    {
      "post_id": "82911",
      "author_handle": "milkymum",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 16 years 11 months ago",
      "body": "Which pregnancy is this? I'n just asking as with my EJ and then the twins I had terrible stomach pains and it was put down to implantation and then when I got past 10 weeks they put it down to early braxton hickes as my stomach muscles hadn't had the full amount of time it takes to heal 100% from having  ababy. It can take between 6 ths right up to 7 years and the more pregnancies you have depending on the age gaps lenghts the healing process. If they get any worse or you start getting blood stained dischareg or any abnormal discharge for you then I would see your doctor ASAP. Hugs and hope it is only implantation cramps and nothing else",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8985/#82911",
